"Software" means the original GeoDolly code, default configuration, and user or developer documentation that a copyright holder distributes under this license. This license does not relicense third-party components, map data, basemap tiles, or fonts. The text of this license and POLICY.md is not Software; you may reproduce these texts unchanged as required for distribution, but editing them does not change the original copyright holders' grant. Project artwork and names have the separate treatment in Sections 7 and 8.

2. Permission

Subject to every condition below, each copyright holder licensing a part of the Software grants you a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free license to access, copy, run, study, modify, and distribute that part, in source or compiled form, solely for Permitted Uses. You may distribute modified versions for Permitted Uses if you identify your changes, preserve copyright and attribution notices, include this LICENSE and POLICY.md, and make clear that your version is unofficial. You may not sublicense the Software or grant recipients broader rights than you received.

3. Permitted Uses

Permitted Uses are personal study and noncommercial use; education and teaching; academic, charitable, and public-interest work; public-sector work and research; and noncommercial modification, testing, and redistribution. A military academy or research institution may use the Software for historical, educational, or other non-operational research. Funding by a government, charity, or research grant does not by itself make otherwise permitted research commercial.

4. Commercial Use is prohibited

"Commercial Use" means using the Software for a commercial product or business operation, a paid or revenue-generating service, paid consulting, work delivered to a commercial client, or a purpose intended to produce a commercial advantage. This includes commercial internal use even when access to the Software itself is free. An institution's name or legal status alone does not determine whether a particular use is permitted. A separate written license from the relevant copyright holder is required for Commercial Use.

5. Operational Military Use is prohibited

"Operational Military Use" means use in, for, or to directly support an actual or planned real-world military operation, including operational planning, target selection, reconnaissance, military intelligence, troop movement or deployment, and operational logistics. The prohibition applies regardless of whether the user calls the activity research, whether the Software is modified, or whether the result is provided to another party. Non-operational teaching and research allowed by Section 3 do not authorize Operational Military Use.

6. Unlawful political activity

You may not use the Software to conduct or knowingly facilitate political propaganda or incitement, broadcasting or communications activity, separatist incitement, or other political activity that is unlawful under the law applicable where the activity is conducted. Political, historical, and geographic research is not prohibited merely because its subject is sensitive or disputed. This section does not require the Software to determine what any jurisdiction's law allows.

